module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.v1_demand_route_refuses_a_module_the_whole_corpus_admission_resolves

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { decl_ref }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

// THE SIBLING OF a_v1_unit_test_red_on_main_runs_in_no_required_lane, on the other v1 surface. That row is a
// v1 test no required lane RUNS; this one is a v1 ROUTE no required lane takes. Found 2026-11-03 by
// clever-carp-493 while converting the drift lanes off `gunbc run --function` (routed by stern-bat-401),
// measured on the same layout with two different builds of the seed. Filed per stern-bat-401's ruling that
// the regression be recorded whether or not it is worked, since v1's semantics are frozen and the lane that
// ran this route is being retired.

data v1_demand_route_refuses_a_module_the_whole_corpus_admission_resolves: RecurringFailureMode =
  RecurringFailureMode {
    identity: "v1_demand_route_refuses_a_module_the_whole_corpus_admission_resolves" as NonEmptyStr,

    // FOUND SILENTLY WRONG, SO BELOW THE LADDER. Two admission routes disagree about which modules exist,
    // and no lane runs both, so the disagreement is not a signal anything receives. The ceiling is
    // MechanicallyPreventable: one lane that admits the corpus both ways and compares the verdicts makes an
    // unnoticed disagreement impossible. The blocker is not knowledge — the bisect is already in the
    // receipts — it is that the required path withdrew the route's last consumer (gunbc.rung_drop
    // v1_required_lanes_withdrawn), so nothing is positioned to notice.
    rung: RungRead {
      found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder,
      standing: BelowCeiling {
        current: FoundBelowTheLadder,
        ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable,
        blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
        trigger_capability: "the capability of one lane to admit the corpus by BOTH routes — the whole-corpus admission the check and the compiled lane use, and the demand-driven resolution `gunbc run --function` performs — and refuse when the two verdicts disagree, SUFFICIENT FOR a checkout where a module resolves under one route and refuses under the other to stop somewhere, instead of the second route's refusal being discovered only by whoever happens to hand-run it"
      },
    },

    receipts: [
      "**INVALID STATE.** The same tree, the same entry, the same function resolves under the whole-corpus admission and refuses under the v1 interpreter's demand-driven route: `error: resolve failed for v2.cli.main; cause: module v2.emission.build_plan_source_boundaries not found for imported symbol module_boundary_source_boundaries`. The corpus is admitted once as a whole by every check and by the compiled lane, and once on demand by `gunbc run --function`; the two routes are not compared anywhere, so a module reachable to one can be invisible to the other indefinitely.",

      "**WHY IT IS NOT A FAILING CHANGE.** Nothing about the demanded module, the importing module, or the corpus is wrong: the whole-corpus route resolves it, the registry check passes over it, and the compiled route runs the same claim green. The refusal reads as a corpus defect and invites the concealment DESIGN section 5 forbids — deleting or rewriting the import to satisfy a route that is itself the outlier. The route's withdrawal is the reason this survived: `gunbc run --function` ran in the drift lane, whose verdict is a row, and required lanes deliberately do not run the v1 suite (gunbc.rung_drop v1_required_lanes_withdrawn).",

      "**SPECIMEN (measured, 2026-11-03).** gunb-ai/gunbc-private run 41648594356, job tier-o-drift: steps 5 through 12 — including building the seed and its compiler — completed green, and step 13 `Compare each Tier O artifact with its authority (read-only)` exited 101 with the refusal above. Reproduction, in the layout that step ran: `gunbc run --function test.claim.product_toolchain_contract_presentation.product_toolchain_contract_presentation_census_matches_live_corpus --entry v2.cli.main --source-root <public dag> --source-root <private overlay dag>` — the exact pre-#15749 public drift-watch shape, with the private overlay admitted because the census corpus spans both repositories. BISECT: a seed binary built at 2499194f4b2 (2026-10-21) PASSes that command; a build at 72beb487208 fails it; SAME layout, so the change is in the interpreter's route, not in the corpus. The demanded module entered the corpus at 3180554242 (2026-10-21, #15577 'Enroll real source boundaries for product toolchain contracts'), and the Oct-21 binary resolves the identical layout — which is what makes the window a regression rather than a long-standing gap.",

      "**SCOPE OF THE DEFECT.** It is in resolution under the demand route, not in the named module, and not in the label's verdict: the claim's own assertion never ran. Any lane that still hands a corpus to `gunbc run --function` shares the exposure. The census of those lanes lives in gunb-ai/gunbc-private#282's body (the heal verify step, the audit packet's Tier O rendering, the projection-drift render, and the private roster gate); each is scheduled onto the compiled route, which is the route that resolves this corpus.",

      "**CEILING: mechanically preventable.** A lane that admits the corpus by both routes and compares verdicts is a decidable control, not a policy question: where the two disagree it stops. Until then the state is invisible rather than absent.",

      "**NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER.** The parity lane named in the trigger capability exists and runs in a required job. It is NOT a v1 fix and does not depend on one: v1's semantics are frozen, and the point of the lane is that a disagreement gets read, not that the minority route is repaired. Whether the demand route itself is repaired, or retired with its last consumer, is decided by the PURPOSE test on whatever still depends on it — not by this row, which builds nothing.",

      "**REVIEW TELL.** A `not found for imported symbol` refusal from a demand-driven route where the whole-corpus check passes on the same tree. Ask which admission route produced the verdict before diagnosing the corpus; the import is usually the innocent half.",

      "**CONSUMPTION.** Read by the derived `recurring_failure_mode_roster`; builds no step.",
    ],

    evidence: [
      decl_ref(module_path: "v2.emission.build_plan_source_boundaries", decl_name: "module_boundary_source_boundaries"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "test.claim.product_toolchain_contract_presentation", decl_name: "product_toolchain_contract_presentation_census_matches_live_corpus"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.rung_drop.v1_required_lanes_withdrawn", decl_name: "v1_required_lanes_withdrawn"),
    ],
  }
